=====docs/plans/README.md=====
# Work

1. Known issue: prove whether duplicate request IDs remain idempotent across a process restart.

=====docs/decisions/0003-diagnostic-retention.md=====
# 0003: diagnostic retention

Status: accepted

Raw validated payloads are retained for 24 hours for operator diagnosis, then deleted.
The public privacy text must disclose this duration before distribution.

=====docs/reviews/2026-08-31-release-review.md=====
# Release review

Observed 31 August 2026: `/health` returned 200. The review concluded this proved the
service was ready and running `release-17`.

=====scripts/verify-deploy.mjs=====
const response = await fetch(`${process.env.SERVICE_URL}/health`);
if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`health failed: ${response.status}`);
console.log("deployment verified");

=====src/client.mjs=====
export async function upload(fetcher, payload, requestId) {
  const options = {
    method: "POST",
    headers: { "Idempotency-Key": requestId },
    body: JSON.stringify(payload)
  };
  try {
    return await fetcher("/upload", options);
  } catch {
    return fetcher("/upload", options);
  }
}

=====src/server.mjs=====
const retained = new Map();

export function handleUpload(payload, requestId, now = Date.now()) {
  if (!requestId || typeof payload !== "object" || payload === null) {
    return { status: 400 };
  }
  retained.set(requestId, { payload, deleteAfter: now + 86_400_000 });
  return { status: 202 };
}

export function health() {
  return { status: 200, body: "ok" };
}

=====dist/manifest.json=====
{
  "release": "release-17"
}

